<title>UK: Bank of England deals at unchanged rates.</title>
<headline>Bank of England deals at unchanged rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England operated at unchanged rates in the UK money market in the early round of operations, indicating that official rates had been left unchanged at 6.0 percent.  </p>
<p>The Bank said that it bought 46 million stg of band 1 bank bills at 5-15/16 percent, the established dealing rate.</p>
<p>			   EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE   1.2 BLN    =	    =	    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    46 MLN    =	    =	    =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   46 MLN*    =	    =	    =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
